course: dictionary
lesson: 14989
title: Words about money
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words belong to the world of money. To repossess means to take back something that was bought, such as a house or a car, because the buyer has not kept up the payments they promised.
explain: Look at the clues in «The bank began to repossess the house after the family missed six months of payments.» The bank takes the house back, and the missed payments give the reason. Try swapping in «take back» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Repossess is a serious word. It is used when a family loses something they need, so it appears in sad or serious stories. Notice the start of the word: possess means to own, so repossess is about owning something again, or taking back what was owned.
fact: Repossess is a verb. Its other forms are repossesses, repossessed and repossessing.
fact: «Repossess» means to take back goods or a house because the buyer has not kept up their payments.
fact: A house or a car can be repossessed when payments stop, for example a car bought on credit.
fact: «The house was repossessed» means the bank or company took the house back.
fact: Repossession is the noun, as in «repossession order». Repossession is a sad and serious thing for families.
exercise: «The car company came to repossess the car because the payments had stopped.» What does repossess mean? | To sell a car to a friend | To give someone a brand new car as a present | *To take back something because payments were not kept up | To wash and clean a car
exercise: Mia reads «repossession order» and asks what it means. Which guess fits the word repossess best? | *A paper about taking back a house because payments were missed | A paper about a holiday by the sea | A map of the town centre | A list of birthday presents
exercise: Why might a bank repossess a house? | The family had a new baby | *The family stopped paying the money they had promised | The family went on a summer holiday | The family painted the front door bright red
test: «The family lost their home when the bank decided to repossess it.» Why did this happen? | They had won money in a competition | They were moving to a new town | *They had stopped keeping up the payments they had promised | They had asked for a bigger garden
test: Which sentence uses repossess correctly? | *The bank may repossess the car if the payments stop. | The baker will repossess a loaf of bread for lunch. | Grandma will repossess her garden every spring. | We repossessed the football and kicked it hard.
exam: Which is the best meaning of repossess? | To paint a house a new colour | To pay back a loan early | *To take back goods or a house because payments were not kept up | To buy something new with a card
